Perfect! I found the bug. The function is using `parts[1]` which is an off-by-one error. It should be `parts[0]` to get the first word (arrays are 0-indexed). Let me fix it:
Now let me verify that all tests pass:
Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was a classic off-by-one error in `src/parse.py:4`. The function was using `parts[1]` to get the first word, but since Python lists are 0-indexed, it should have been `parts[0]`. This caused:
- `test_basic` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to crash with an IndexError when there was only one word

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
